list.item:
Ball, William L., Assistant Secretary of State
                        for Legislative Affairs from April 2, 1985, until February 28, 1986;
                        President’s Assistant for Legislative Affairs from 1986 until 1988

Brooks, Linton F., Captain, USN (Ret.);
                        Director, Defense Programs, Defense Programs and Arms Control Directorate,
                        National Security Council Staff, from 1986

Carlucci, Frank C., III, President’s Assistant
                        for National Security Affairs from December 2, 1986, until November 23,
                        1987; Secretary of Defense from November 23, 1987

Cobb, Tyrus P., Lieutenant Colonel, USA (Ret,);
                        Director, European and Soviet Affairs Directorate, National Security Council
                        Staff, until 1988

Glitman, Maynard (Mike), U.S. Ambassador and
                        Chief Negotiator on Intermediate-Range Nuclear Arms until June 22, 1988;
                        U.S. Ambassador to Belgium from June 22, 1988

Goldwater, Barry, Senator (R–Arizona);
                        Chairman, Senate Armed Services Committee, from January 3, 1985, until
                        January 3, 1987

Lamberson, Donald L., Major General, USAF;
                        Assistant Deputy Chief of Research, Development, and Acquisition, U.S. Air
                        Force, until 1987

Mathias, Charles, Senator (R–Maryland);
                        President, North Atlantic Treaty Organization Parliamentary Assembly from
                        1985 until 1986

McFarlane, Robert (Bud), Colonel, USMC (Ret.);
                        President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs until December 4,
                        1985

Pell, Claiborne, Senator (D–Rhode Island);
                        Ranking Member, Senate Armed Services Committee, until January 1987;
                        Chairman, Senate Foreign Relations Committee, from January 3, 1987

Poindexter, John M., Rear Admiral, USN;
                        President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs until November 25,
                        1986

